                <pb facs="0325" n="316" sameAs="frus:frus1938v05/pg316"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">835.248/98: Telegram</note>
                <head><hi rendition="#italic">The Ambassador in Brazil</hi> (<hi rendition="#italic">Caffery</hi>) <hi
                        rendition="#italic">to the Secretary of
                    State</hi></head>
                <opener>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right"><placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps">Rio de
                                Janeiro</hi></placeName>, <date calendar="gregorian"
                            when="1938-05-11T13:00:00-03:00">May 11, 1938—1
                        p.m.</date><lb/>[Received May 11—12:25 p.m.]</dateline>
                </opener>
                <p>106. For the Under Secretary. Second paragraph Department’s telegram 47, April 1,
                    6 p.m. Associated Press despatch from Buenos Aires published here asserts that
                    the Argentine Government has contracted for the services of American military
                    instructors in aviation and that they are to leave Washington for Buenos Aires
                    within the next few days. The officers are said to be specialists in night
                    flights and aerial bombardment. This despatch is attracting considerable
                    attention here.</p>
                <p>I would appreciate any pertinent information.</p>
                <closer><signed><hi rendition="#small-caps">Caffery</hi></signed></closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
